From: Parthiban Nallathambi <parthiban@linumiz.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:23:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] gdb: v850: Add the G4 and FXU registers

Name the RH850 G4 system registers, use the target description that
QEMU provides, and map the GCC DWARF numbers of the FXU registers.

Signed-off-by: Parthiban Nallathambi <parthiban@linumiz.com>
---
 gdb/doc/gdb.texinfo |  24 ++-
 gdb/v850-tdep.c     | 370 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 2 files changed, 311 insertions(+), 83 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gdb/doc/gdb.texinfo b/gdb/doc/gdb.texinfo
index a6e1f114320..7ad394be980 100644
--- a/gdb/doc/gdb.texinfo
+++ b/gdb/doc/gdb.texinfo
@@ -10478,7 +10478,7 @@ The default value is the empty string.
 If it is necessary to specify more than one disassembler option, then
 multiple options can be placed together into a comma separated list.
 Currently this command is only supported on targets ARC, ARM, MIPS,
-PowerPC and S/390.
+PowerPC, S/390 and V850.
 
 @kindex show disassembler-options
 @item show disassembler-options
@@ -49332,6 +49332,7 @@ registers using the capitalization used in the description.
 * S/390 and System z Features::
 * Sparc Features::
 * TIC6x Features::
+* V850 Features::
 @end menu
 
 
@@ -50518,6 +50519,27 @@ through @samp{B31}.
 The @samp{org.gnu.gdb.tic6x.c6xp} feature is optional.  It should
 contain registers @samp{TSR}, @samp{ILC} and @samp{RILC}.
 
+@node V850 Features
+@subsection V850 Features
+@cindex target descriptions, V850 features
+
+The @samp{org.gnu.gdb.v850.core} feature is optional for v850e3v5
+targets.  It should contain the registers of the fixed v850e3v5
+register layout of @value{GDBN}, in order, with their v850e3v5 names:
+@samp{r0} through @samp{r31}, the system registers, @samp{pc} and
+@samp{vr0} through @samp{vr31}.  A register number that has no name in
+that layout is called @samp{unused@var{n}}, where @var{n} is the
+register number.  When this feature is present and complete,
+@value{GDBN} uses the target description, and registers in other
+features, for example system registers with a selection ID of 8 or
+more, are shown with the names that the target gives them.  Without
+the feature, @value{GDBN} uses the fixed layout.
+
+If the target description has registers named @samp{wr0} through
+@samp{wr31} (the RH850 FXU registers), @value{GDBN} maps the DWARF
+register numbers 36 through 67 that GCC uses for them to these
+registers.
+
 @node Operating System Information
 @appendix Operating System Information
 @cindex operating system information
